vr overlay 0037 — the 64-light mask: BIT_ULL, and a light list that belongs to its own batch

The reported artefact: walls and floors switch lighter/darker as the player moves,
sometimes in one eye only. Device-confirmed on 1.0.11.14 (base1, rerelease data):
`gl_dynamic 0` stops it; `gl_dynamic 1` + `gl_per_pixel_lighting 0` also stops it — so
it is the per-pixel light path, and neither the lightmap side nor lightstyles.

M1. `glr.ppl_dlight_bits` is `uint64_t` and MAX_DLIGHTS is 64, but two sites build and
test it with `1 << n` on an `int`. n == 31 yields INT_MIN, which sign-extends on the
conversion to uint64_t and admits light 31 whenever ANY of bits 31..63 is set; n >= 32
shifts past the width of int (undefined, and arm64's 32-bit LSL wraps the count mod 32),
so light 32 is gated by bit 0, light 33 by bit 1, ... light 63 by bit 31. The marking
side is already correct 64-bit (`world.c` BIT_ULL), so these two are the only places the
top half of the mask is lost.

Why it moves with the head: a world batch's bits are the union of its faces' dlightbits,
and batch composition is a function of the view. Move, and the union's LOW bits change —
which admits or drops a HIGH light that has nothing to do with them. A wall light
vanishes, the wall steps darker, and steps back when the batch changes again. The two
eyes have different frusta, so the same argument makes it one-eye-only.

Why the simulator cannot reproduce it: original-baseq2 carries no shadowlight
configstrings, so num_dlights stays at 0-3 and n never reaches 31. The rerelease's
CL_AddShadowLights appends every live shadowlight, and a base1 room passes 31 easily.

M3. `glr.ppl_dlight_bits` is global and was assigned only when the batch had marked
lights, so a batch with none carried the LAST ALIAS MODEL's light list — which
GL_LoadLights keys its UBO upload on. Assigned unconditionally in GL_Flush3D, the value
belongs to the batch being drawn and nothing else.

Both are upstream bugs, not port-local ones, and the fix is upstreamable as-is.

--- a/src/refresh/shader.c
+++ b/src/refresh/shader.c
@@ -1032,7 +1032,15 @@
     c.dlightsTotal += nl;
 
     for (int n = 0; n < nl; n++) {
-        if (!(glr.ppl_dlight_bits & 1 << n)) {
+        // [vr overlay 0037] BIT_ULL, not `1 << n`. glr.ppl_dlight_bits is uint64_t and
+        // MAX_DLIGHTS is 64, but `1` here is int: n == 31 makes 1 << 31 == INT_MIN, which
+        // sign-extends to 0xFFFFFFFF80000000 and admits light 31 whenever ANY of bits 31-63
+        // is set, and n >= 32 is a shift past the width of int - undefined, and on arm64 the
+        // count wraps mod 32, so light 32 is gated by bit 0, light 33 by bit 1, and so on.
+        // The marking side is already correct 64-bit (world.c BIT_ULL), so this is the one
+        // place the mask loses its top half. Upstream bug; the rerelease reaches index 31+
+        // routinely because CL_AddShadowLights appends every live shadowlight to r_dlights.
+        if (!(glr.ppl_dlight_bits & BIT_ULL(n))) {
             c.dlightsNotUsed++;
             continue;
         }
--- a/src/refresh/mesh.c
+++ b/src/refresh/mesh.c
@@ -998,7 +998,7 @@
             continue;
         }
 
-        glr.ppl_dlight_bits |= 1 << i;
+        glr.ppl_dlight_bits |= BIT_ULL(i);   // [vr overlay 0037] same 64-bit mask, same defect
     }
 }
 
--- a/src/refresh/tess.c
+++ b/src/refresh/tess.c
@@ -791,10 +791,14 @@
                 state |= GLS_GLOWMAP_ENABLE;
         }
 
-        if (tess.dlight_bits && glr.ppl_bits) {
-            glr.ppl_dlight_bits = tess.dlight_bits;
+        // [vr overlay 0037] ASSIGNED UNCONDITIONALLY. glr.ppl_dlight_bits is global state:
+        // GL_DrawAliasModel rebuilds it per mesh and nothing puts the world's value back, and
+        // the old guarded assignment left a batch with no marked lights carrying the LAST
+        // MESH's light list - which GL_LoadLights then keys the UBO upload on. Assigning it
+        // here every flush makes the value belong to the batch being drawn and nothing else.
+        glr.ppl_dlight_bits = tess.dlight_bits;
+        if (tess.dlight_bits && glr.ppl_bits)
             state |= glr.ppl_bits;
-        }
         array |= GLA_NORMAL;
     }
 
